on":"relates_to","target_id":"bf7c-333e-29b0-4ee4"},{"link_uuid":"0eb7b68b-208b-4569-a470-b3ffe6fc8152","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fb03-2609-ef83-4b41"},{"link_uuid":"0640be86-1f80-4ebb-8ba2-6cd9dfeaa262","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5"},{"link_uuid":"d0f1c26c-3267-4f13-9a14-f06999757b16","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f"}],"description":"## Context\nF12 verification on commit 8a036765705f5ef0e7db4fa21e0926e51d15bafd exposed a long-running `test_resign_routes_through_pin_collecting_sign_path`. An isolated run on current `origin/main` commit 51621917bfc635d7673cb0519a400afda12eb2cb reproduced the delay. The test body reported PASS after 201.81 seconds. The process exited after 524.52 seconds. Pytest attributed 5.15 seconds to setup and 0.06 seconds to teardown. A one-second process sample during the remaining post-PASS interval showed recursive filesystem deletion dominated by `unlinkat` and `rmdir`.\n\nClosed tickets `grindable-deviant-angwantibo` and `asbestos-popular-tench` repaired omitted private `--basetemp` arguments in nested pytest children. This reproduction occurs in an ordinary test session and needs separate lifecycle tracing. Active ticket `famished-disgustful-gypsymoth` changes timeout coverage for fixture phases. Active ticket `expectable-slowwitted-squeaker` covers a local Git child timeout. Neither ticket records this test or its post-PASS deletion interval.\n\n## Plan\n- Reproduce the delay in an isolated current-main worktree and capture phase timings, the active temporary path, file counts, allocated bytes, and a Python stack during the post-PASS interval.\n- Trace the fixture and pytest lifecycle that creates and removes the snapshot tree.\n- Distinguish test-call snapshot materialization cost, session-finish cleanup cost, shared temporary-root cleanup, and host filesystem contention with discriminating experiments.\n- Determine whether pending Gerrit change 2141 guards the affected phase or only changes the terminal failure mode.\n- Establish the intended behavior from the maintained timeout and test-runtime policy.\n- Confirm the root cause and defect origin before proposing any repair.\n- If a repair is warranted, update this ticket with the fix plan and file impact, obtain a current plan review, and prove the repair with a RED-first held-out oracle.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A current-main reproduction records call time, total time, and the post-PASS stack.\n- [ ] Runtime evidence identifies the lifecycle phase and the changeable artifact responsible for the delay.\n- [ ] Discriminating experiments reject the surviving alternative explanations.\n- [ ] The relationship to `grindable-deviant-angwantibo`, `asbestos-popular-tench`, `famished-disgustful-gypsymoth`, and `expectable-slowwitted-squeaker` is recorded.\n- [ ] The defect origin is proven or the RCA records the completed unattributable search.\n- [ ] The RCA is recorded before any repair begins.\n- [ ] Any repair uses a RED-first oracle, preserves unrelated test behavior, and passes its declared verification.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","797b-bbc4-01cf-42d5"],["relates_to","bd66-28a4-fd31-4c9f"],["relates_to","bf7c-333e-29b0-4ee4"],["relates_to","fb03-2609-ef83-4b41"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"Phase 1 diagnosis only. No edit path is authorized until the root cause is confirmed and the repair plan is reviewed.","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["debugging","performance","tests"],"ticket_id":"8908-043d-c697-4493","ticket_type":"bug","title":"pytest session cleanup spends minutes deleting plan-review snapshot tree","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["f8ed394b-7745-4010-96d5-95085df99c83","683cffdd-d1ab-496c-b26a-f3dfeab059a